                <pb facs="0237" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg197"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1293.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 9, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 16th of February last, No.879. In connexion with that
                    paper you give me a <pb facs="0238" n="198" xml:id="pg198"/> copy of a
                    correspondence which has passed between yourself and Earl Russell on the subject
                    of outfits of vessels for account of rebels, described in a schedule annexed to
                    your despatch, as follows:</p>


                <xi:include href="d111-a1.xml" xpointer="d111-a1"/>
            </div>
